WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:05.820
Once upon a time, Jessica Alba seemed poised
for superstardom, tearing up both television

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:09.990
and movies with a series of hits that had
fans screaming for more.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:14.839
Beautiful, talented, popular — what didn't
Alba seem to have going for her?

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:18.930
But instead of an unstoppable career, she
suddenly dropped off the map.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:23.160
Here's a look at why Hollywood won't cast
Jessica Alba anymore.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.590
The Invisible Woman

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:29.730
Alba's biggest claim to fame is probably her
role in 2005's Sin City, where she shared

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:34.230
the screen with a huge ensemble cast that
included mega-stars like Bruce Willis and

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.300
Clive Owen.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.110
Sin City proved to be a massive hit, but her
reign at the top was incredibly brief, because

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:43.600
just a couple months later, Fantastic Four
came out.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:48.800
Though it was a modest box office success,
critics savaged the film, and the experience

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.640
of making it caused Alba to re-evaluate whether
she even wanted to be an actress at all after

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:59.140
director Tim Story berated her for actually
acting too well during a crying scene.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:00.920
"God, really?!"

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:06.210
Instead, he wanted to actually add tears in
post-production using CGI.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:10.540
Alba told Elle, "It all got me thinking: Am
I not good enough?

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.300
Are my instincts and my emotions not good
enough?

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:16.640
Do people hate them so much that they don't
want me to be a person?

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.230
Am I not allowed to be a person in my work?

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:20.810
And so I just said, 'F*** it.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:24.030
I don't care about this business anymore.'"

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:28.580
That may explain why Alba hasn't made a memorable
movie since.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:29.580
Exotic

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.740
Hollywood hasn't always had the greatest track
record when it comes to casting diversity,

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:39.070
so you may not be surprised to hear that Alba's
choice of roles has been limited by her heritage.

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:44.290
She told PopSugar that she wasn't considered
Caucasian enough to play white roles, or Hispanic

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.050
enough to play Latina roles.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:51.979
"And then when I did start, you know, getting
a lot of roles and auditioning, they couldn't

00:01:51.979 --> 00:01:52.979
figure out my ethnicity.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:55.830
So they would --- I would always go out for
'exotic.'"

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.870
So much for show business being color blind.

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:00.030
The bomb squad

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:03.470
It's safe to say that Alba's films don't always
get good reviews.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:04.470
Or often.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:05.830
Or, like… ever.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:11.190
In fact, of the 29 movies she's made that
have enough reviews to qualify for a Rotten

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.910
Tomatoes score, only three of them have a
fresh rating, which is kind of incredible.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:20.250
Mathematically speaking, you'd expect random
chance would give her at least a few decent

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.250
roles.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:25.209
And over the years, Alba herself has been
singled out for being particularly bad in

00:02:25.209 --> 00:02:32.819
those films, landing Razzie nominations in
2006, 2008, 2009, and 2011, when she finally

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:35.280
won for Worst Supporting Actress.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:39.470
Which is understandable given even she seems
a little confused at times just what role

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:40.860
she's supposed to be playing.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.940
"We also both know that I'm just not anybody.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.040
Am I Dumbledore?"

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.650
No, Jessica, this is Dumbledore.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:51.810
Business before pleasure

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:56.110
After becoming disillusioned with the film
industry, Alba turned her attention in other

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.760
directions, such as raising her two children.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:03.930
In 2008, after using a popular detergent specifically
for kids, one of her children developed a

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.390
painful rash.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:10.280
The incident inspired Alba to found The Honest
Company, which makes affordable, environmentally

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:13.030
friend, non-toxic household goods.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:18.760
The Honest Company officially launched in
2011, and by 2015, was valued at nearly two

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:19.760
billion dollars.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.640
It hasn't all been organic roses, though.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:27.620
In 2016, the Wall Street Journal accused The
Honest Company of false advertising, and the

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.420
company has faced multiple lawsuits.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:33.440
Alba chalks it up to the downside of being
a celebrity.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:39.170
"If an organization wants to bring awareness
to their cause, I'm an easy target and our

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.230
brand is an easy target..."

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:42.480
Don't call it a comeback

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.570
Despite everything, Alba has been keeping
her foot in the door by appearing in smaller

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:47.570
film roles.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:50.080
And she still has a large fan following.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:53.849
So it's not a matter of whether she can make
a comeback, it's just a question of whether

00:03:53.849 --> 00:03:54.849
she wants too.

00:03:54.849 --> 00:03:56.080
"you still haven't greenlit

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:58.170
my passion project!"

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:01.901
While she has said in the past that she's
open to doing more movies in the future, it

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:06.060
seems like it'll take the perfect film to
bring her out of semi-retirement.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:09.470
In other words: don't call her, Hollywood,
she'll call you.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:10.860
Thanks for watching!

